-- title:
--   High-cusp unfolding bound in Iwasawa coordinates
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $\alpha,\beta$ be reals with $0<\alpha$ and $\alpha<\beta$. The assertion is the existence of a constant $c_0\in[0,\infty]$ with $c_0\neq\infty$ such that the following holds. Let $D,D'$ be measurable subsets of the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$, each a fundamental domain, for the idelic Haar measure [`NumberField.Idele.idelicHaar`](def/NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure.html#L391), for the subgroup of principal ideles, namely the image of $K^\times$ under the map induced by $K\to\mathbb{A}_K$. Let $T\in\mathbb{R}$ and let $F\colon GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to[0,\infty]$ be measurable and invariant under left translation by every element of `rationalTorusUnipotent K`, the subgroup generated by the rational centre, the rational elements $\mathrm{diag}(t,1)$ and the full adelic unipotent subgroup. Then the integral of $F$ against the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` over the intersection of the canonical truncation domain attached to $(\alpha,\beta)$ (the second set component of the canonical truncation datum, a fundamental domain for the global points inside the determinant slab by [`AutomorphicForm.canonicalTruncationData_isTruncationDatum`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.canonicalTruncationData_isTruncationDatum)) with the high-height region $\{g : T<H(g)\}$, where $H$ is the adelic height, is at most $c_0$ times $$\int_{D}\int_{D'}\int_{\mathbf K}\bigl(\mathbf 1_{\{\alpha\le|\det g|_{\mathbb A}\le\beta\}\cap\{T<H(g)\}}F\bigr)\bigl(z\cdot\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\cdot k\bigr)\,|t|_{\mathbb A}^{-1}\,dk\,d^\times t\,d^\times z,$$ where $z$ runs over $D$ as a central scalar, $t$ over $D'$, $k$ over the adelic maximal compact subgroup with its Haar measure `maximalCompactHaar`, and $|\cdot|_{\mathbb A}$ denotes the idele norm. The constant is not asserted to be non-zero.
--
--   This is the one-sided (inequality) half of the classical unfolding of the cuspidal part of a fundamental domain for $GL_2(K)$ onto the Borel quotient, written in Iwasawa coordinates: the high-height portion of the truncation domain is dominated by an integral over central ideles, the split torus coordinate and the maximal compact, with the modulus factor $|t|_{\mathbb A}^{-1}$. It feeds the subsequent reduction of the high-cusp contribution to a one-dimensional integral over a half-line in the torus variable.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_forall_setLIntegral_canonicalTruncationDomain_inter_lt_adelicHeight_le_mul_setLIntegral_iwasawa_indicator.lean

